In triangle $PQR$, $\overrightarrow{PQ}=2\underset{\sim}{a}$ and $\overrightarrow{PR}=3\underset{\sim}{b}$. The point $M$ is the midpoint of $QR$. Find (a) $\overrightarrow{QM}$ and (b) $\overrightarrow{PM}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0); \coordinate (Q) at (1,3); \coordinate (R) at (5,0); \coordinate (M) at (3,1.5);
\draw[black,thick,->] (P)--(Q) node[midway,left] {$2\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\draw[black,thick,->] (P)--(R) node[midway,below] {$3\underset{\sim}{b}$};
\draw[black] (Q)--(R); \fill[black] (M) circle (1.5pt);
\path (P) node[below left] {$P$} (Q) node[above] {$Q$} (R) node[below right] {$R$} (M) node[above right] {$M$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
(a) Subtract the two vectors with common tail $P$, then halve the result.
$\begin{aligned}\overrightarrow{QR}&=\overrightarrow{PR}-\overrightarrow{PQ}\\&=3\underset{\sim}{b}-2\underset{\sim}{a}\end{aligned}$
$\begin{aligned}\overrightarrow{QM}&=\frac{1}{2}\overrightarrow{QR}\\&=\frac{3}{2}\underset{\sim}{b}-\underset{\sim}{a}\end{aligned}$
(b) Use the route $P\to Q\to M$.
$\begin{aligned}\overrightarrow{PM}&=\overrightarrow{PQ}+\overrightarrow{QM}\\&=2\underset{\sim}{a}+\frac{3}{2}\underset{\sim}{b}-\underset{\sim}{a}\\&=\underset{\sim}{a}+\frac{3}{2}\underset{\sim}{b}\end{aligned}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{solutionBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\coordinate (P) at (0,0); \coordinate (Q) at (1,3); \coordinate (R) at (5,0); \coordinate (M) at (3,1.5);
\draw[black,thick,->] (P)--(Q) node[midway,left] {$2\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\draw[black,thick,->] (P)--(R) node[midway,below] {$3\underset{\sim}{b}$};
\draw[black] (Q)--(R);
\draw[solutionBlue,thick,->] (Q)--(M);
\draw[solutionBlue,thick,->] (P)--(M);
\fill[black] (M) circle (1.5pt);
\path (P) node[below left] {$P$} (Q) node[above] {$Q$} (R) node[below right] {$R$} (M) node[above right] {$M$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

